  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A uniform capillary tube of inner radius <math><mi>r</mi></math> is dipped vertically into a beaker filled with water. The water rises to a height <math><mi>h</mi></math> in the capillary tube above the water surface in the beaker. The surface tension of water is <math><mi>&#963;</mi></math> . The angle of contact between water and the wall of the capillary tube is <math><mi>&#952;</mi></math> . Ignore the mass of water in the meniscus. Which of the following statements is (are) true?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "BDcDH",
      "text": "For a given material of the capillary tube, <math><mi>h</mi></math> decreases with increase in <math><mi>r</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "bgINK",
      "text": "For a given material of the capillary tube,  <math><mi>h</mi></math>  is independent of  <math><mi>σ</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "arrGN",
      "text": "If this experiment is performed in a lift going up with a constant acceleration, then <math><mi>h</mi></math> decreases",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q99TH",
      "text": "<math><mi>h</mi></math>  is proportional to contact angle  <math><mi>θ</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></math> <math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> <math><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></math> [r→radius of capillary; <math><mi>θ</mi><mo>→</mo></math> contact angle]<br /><math><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></math> For given material, <math><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math><br /><math><mi>h</mi><mo>∝</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo></math> h depends on <math><mi>σ</mi></math><br /><math><mo>(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo></math> If lift is going up with constant acceleration,<br /><math><msub><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math> It means h decreases<br /><math><mo>(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>)</mo></math> h is proportional to <math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>θ</mi></math>",
